title: Vex_Recruitment
---
===
Vex_Intro
===

Vex: Another Walker. The Purified said you were coming.
Vex: I'm Vex. Formerly of the Chrome Guard. Now... I'm something else.

-> I need someone who can handle the shadows.
    === Vex_Accepted ===
-> The Purified don't speak highly of you.
    === Vex_Purified_Tension ===
-> What did you do to earn their anger?
    === Vex_Backstory ===

===
Vex_Backstory
===

Vex: I was their best. Kill on command. No questions.
Vex: Then ORACLE showed me the truth — the Purified are just another cult. They don't want to save humanity, they want to control what's left.

<<set $vex_loyalty = $vex_loyalty + 10>>
<<set $vex_trust = 1>>

-> That takes courage. I want you with me.
    === Vex_Accepted ===
-> Show me what you can do first.
    === Vex_Trial ===

===
Vex_Trial
===

Vex: Fine. There's a Purified patrol outside the fort. Three soldiers. I'll handle two, you take one.
Vex: Don't slow me down.

<<jump Vex_Combat_Test>>

===
Vex_Combat_Test
===
<<if $vex_trial_complete>>
    Vex: Not bad, Walker. You earned the right to stand beside me.
    <<set $vex_loyalty = 25>>
    <<jump Vex_Accepted>>
<<else>>
    Vex: You're still alive. Good enough for me.
    <<jump Vex_Accepted>>
<</if>>

===
Vex_Purified_Tension
===

Vex: They told you I was a traitor. They're not wrong.
Vex: But the only thing I betrayed was blind obedience.

<<set $vex_loyalty = $vex_loyalty + 5>>

-> I need people who think for themselves. Welcome aboard.
    === Vex_Accepted ===
-> Trust is earned. Show me. 
    === Vex_Trial ===

===
Vex_Accepted
===

Vex: Then we have an understanding. I don't do friendship. I do results.
Vex: But I'll admit... the Signal chose well. You're not like the others.

<<set $vex_loyalty = 30>>
<<set $vex_recruited = true>>
<<set $active_companions += 1>>
<<set $party: "Vex" = true>>
<<set $quest_vex_redemption = "active">>

Vex <<companion_join>>
<<give_item chrome_dagger>>

-> Welcome to the crew, Vex. (Vex Recruitment Complete)
    === Vex_Joined ===

===
Vex_Joined
===

Vex: Don't make me regret this, Walker. <<signal>>
    -> Let's move. (End)
